0..65 Comment "// A program reads the release metrics of the exact reals through"
66..140 Comment "// `std.reals.Eff`, the host interface of exact reals. `report` gives nine"
141..216 Comment "// counters of a machine in a fixed order. `gandr run metrics.gandr` prints"
217..288 Comment "// `the metrics hold`. The same `measured` runs under a handler of this"
289..332 Comment "// source, a second model of the interface."
333..335 Comment "//"
336..406 Comment "// The first three counters are the work of a machine: its quanta, its"
407..485 Comment "// obligations and the steps of its certificate. The other six are the metrics"
486..565 Comment "// of the first release: the frontier, the cache hits, the regions, the checker"
566..642 Comment "// steps, the checkpoints and the cancellations. A program compares two runs"
643..680 Comment "// by them, apart from the wall time."
681..683 Comment "//"
684..767 Comment "// The program decides `∃ x ∈ [1, 2] (3 < x · x)` within 32 quanta. Its search"
768..846 Comment "// holds at most 4 pieces at once, and the checker replays the 13 steps of its"
847..924 Comment "// certificate. The program then stops `sqrt 2 < 3/2` after one quantum, with"
925..1003 Comment "// two poles live, and spells its checkpoint. The restore replays the one step"
1004..1081 Comment "// of the checkpoint. The host consults no cache and signals no cancellation,"
1082..1110 Comment "// so those counts are zero."
1111..1113 Comment "//"
1114..1192 Comment "// - see: `corpus/model/reals/resume.gandr` — the checkpoint and the restore"
1193..1268 Comment "// - see: `crates/surface-dispatcher/src/evaluate/reals/machine.rs` — the"
1269..1295 Comment "//   counters of a machine"
1297..1329 Comment "// The console\'s host interface."
